---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = '2026-05-06';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — OneBrain"
  description="OneBrain runs locally on your machine. Here's the short list of what we don't store, what we do, and how to reach us."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="legal-section">
      <div class="legal-shell">
        <header class="legal-head">
          <div class="cyber-pill">
            <span class="cyber-pill-dot"></span>
            <span>ONEBRAIN // LEGAL</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="legal-h1">Privacy.</h1>
          <p class="legal-meta">UPDATED {updated} · APPLIES TO onebrain.run + @onebrain-ai/cli</p>
        </header>

        <article class="legal-prose">
          <p>
            <strong class="brand">OneBrain</strong> runs locally on your machine —
            self-hosted from your terminal, a built-in web UI, or inside Obsidian.
            Your notes, your agent's memory, your conversations — none of it leaves
            your machine. The CLI talks directly to your LLM provider of choice;
            OneBrain reads and writes plain Markdown files on your disk. We don't
            have a server in that loop.
          </p>

          <h2>What we don't store</h2>
          <p>
            Vault contents. Agent memory. Prompts. Session logs. Skill output.
            We never see any of it. There's no telemetry pipeline, no
            cloud-backed analytics on what you write or how you use the agent.
          </p>

          <h2>What we do store</h2>
          <p>
            The one place you hand us data is the email you give us to be
            notified when OneBrain Sync ships. The row holds: your email,
            the time you signed up, and a hash of your IP (salted with a
            private string and truncated — the raw IP is never written).
            That's it. No tracking pixels, no third-party analytics, no
            embedded scripts shipped to the page from anywhere except this
            domain.
          </p>
          <p>
            OneBrain is self-hosted and open source (MIT / Apache-2.0) — there's
            no hosted service in the loop, so there's nothing else to collect.
            The only record we hold is the notify-me row keyed by your email.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions, deletion requests, GDPR/CCPA asks, or anything else —
            email <a href="mailto:hello@onebrain.run">hello@onebrain.run</a>
            and we'll respond within a few business days.
          </p>
        </article>

        <p class="legal-back">
          <a href="/">← back to onebrain.run</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-section {
    /* The cyber-pill in <header> reads `var(--section-accent)` for its
       color/background/border — without a value here, color-mix() can't
       resolve and the pill collapses to just its corner brackets +
       dot. Set the accent (the cyber-pill reads --section-accent; .legal-prose a, .legal-prose h2, and .legal-back a:hover hard-code the same #c8ff00 — keep them in sync). */
    --section-accent: #c8ff00;

    position: relative;
    min-height: calc(100vh - 80px);
    /* Top padding only needs to clear the 64px sticky nav + a little
       breathing room — 8rem left an unnecessary blank band above the
       title. */
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    background: #050507;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  }

  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-head { margin-bottom: 3rem; }

  .legal-h1 {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-family: 'Chakra Petch', var(--font-display), sans-serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  }

  .legal-prose {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', var(--font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
  }
  .legal-prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .legal-prose h2 {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #c8ff00;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200, 255, 0, 0.18);
  }
  .legal-prose strong.brand {
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
  }
  .legal-prose a {
    color: #c8ff00;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(200, 255, 0, 0.4);
    transition: color 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .legal-prose a:hover {
    color: #fff;
    border-bottom-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .legal-back {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .legal-back a {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .legal-back a:hover { color: #c8ff00; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-section { padding: 3rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
    .legal-prose { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; }
  }
</style>
